cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark dataset, please cite both the dataset itself (using the metadata below) and the accompanying peer-reviewed paper (see 'preferred-citation')."
type: dataset
title: "SimilCode Benchmark: A Dual-Language Source-Code Similarity Dataset for the Evaluation of AI-Based Detectors"
abstract: >
  SimilCode Benchmark is a controlled dataset of 120 source-code pairs in C#
  and Java (15 reference programs per language, four similarity categories:
  identical, functional, structural and different) for evaluating source-code
  similarity detectors. It includes the raw results of a replicated
  evaluation of four commercial large language models (GPT-5.5,
  DeepSeek-V4-pro, Gemini 3.1 Pro and Claude Opus 5; 1,440 evaluations,
  three replicas per pair and model), the outputs of Moss, JPlag and Dolos on
  the same pairs, the validation corpus and predictions of the Big O
  estimator, and a script that reproduces every number of the companion
  manuscript.
version: 2.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-21"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/gleiston-guerrero/SimilCode-Benchmark"
